next question today is from RJ RJ says  hey David how can we combat statements  like black people are brainwashed by the  Democrats from the right okay so this  there's a lot tied up in this question  if you have not heard that statement  before that's great  I wish I had also never heard it but the  idea of the brainwashing of voting  groups implies that you have a group of  people an identity group that votes for  one party or the other despite the fact  that they would actually be better off  by supporting the other party based on  the policy right so like with black  voters what the Republicans have been  claiming is black voters have been  brainwashed into voting for Democrats  even though they would be better off by  supporting Republicans because you have  to demonstrate that otherwise black  people are just voting for Democrats  because the policies of Democrats could  be or are better for black people which  I believe is actually the case so to  start examining this the first question  you have to ask is okay on which issue  is the Republican policy better overall  for black Americans than the Democratic  policy and I can't think of any such  policy you will hear people from the  right who say that affirmative action is  actually bad for minorities because it  is an example of the bigotry of saw of  low expectations the soft bigotry of low  expectations is the way they like to  describe it I believe that there is no  factual case to be made that that has  been the impact of affirmative action in  places where it exists and remembered  that in most places affirmative action  does not actually exist in the way that  is described by the right so unless you  can actually sit link some specific  policies of the rights with lack of  support for Republicans by black people  the even mere claim on its face that  black people have been quote brainwashed  by Democrats Falls pretty flat now in  fact when you think about it there's a  much stronger case to be made that poor  and lower middle class right-wingers are  the ones who have been brain  washed by the Republican Party and I  think back to the Tea Party in 2010 you  had people who statistically will never  be rich  statistically will never earn two  hundred and fifty thousand dollars a  year which I think was the tax bracket  sort of in question at the time that the  Tea Party really wanted to lower the  marginal tax rate on saying we support  the Tea Party despite the fact that the  policies would be great for rich people  and not good for lower and lower middle  class and even middle class Americans so  if you want to see political  brainwashing it's all the people on the  right that insist on voting Republicans  against their own best interests now let  me go to a counter example to the black  people are brainwashed by Democrats meme  when California had a referendum vote  called Proposition 8 around gay marriage  which was widely supported by Democrats  you didn't see black people come out in  droves to support gay marriage in  California so it's almost like black  people can understand that on most  issues Democrats actually have the right  slate of policies to improve their  circumstances but they're not just going  to go out and vote for gay marriage  merely because Democrats wanted the  black population at the time and still  to some degree has more skepticism of  gay marriage and homophobia within  within its borders and that was very  much reflected in Proposition 8 mostly  they vote with Democrats but they broke  with many Democrats on that particular  issue I I do want to point out also  there's a bit of an implicit racism in  saying that because Republicans are very  United as a voting bloc nationally they  are brainwashed but that same standard  is not applied to other groups I'll give  you an example Jews in the United States  are very liberal Jews vote depending on  the election seventy-five to eighty  percent with Democrats with the more  liberal candidate with the more  progressive candidate whatever if  anything you hear the opposite which is  that Jew  brainwashed by the pro-israeli antics of  the right well if they are it seems to  have failed or confuse them because  they're almost exclusively voting for  Democrats but you don't really hear that  word applied so my instinct Pat is that  there is some implicit racism in saying  that the United voting bloc not  completely but significantly if black  people is a brainwashing but it's not  applied to other groups and might I add  if you're a Republican strategist and  you're trying to pick off some  african-american voters and persuade  them to vote with your side it's a  really bad idea to be condescending and  start saying that they're brainwashed  like that's that's not going to work out  for you  no I completely agree with you  and then there's also the issue of sort  of conservatism pushing individualism in  many ways and black Americans like many  other groups have a strong group  identity which goes beyond policy and it  would be another reason to favor  generally collectivist policies and in  the United States to the extent that  there is a difference between Democrats  and Republicans on that Democrats are  the ones advocating for the more  collectivist policies than Republicans  and that would be a very specific  political reason why you would see black  Americans support Democrats more than  Republicans so there's really simply no  evidence for this brainwashing that the  right claims exists
 

